---
term: Coordination principle
section: principles
order: 20
definition: The principle that higher-order charters resolve conflicts among lower-order charters according to their own higher-order common interest.
seeAlso:
  - escalation
  - arbitration
  - higher-order-common-interest
---
Conflict isn't eliminated. It moves up to the level whose charter covers every party involved, and that level uses its own purpose as the standard for resolving it.

> Let higher-order charters coordinate conflicts among lower-order charters according to their own higher-order common interest.
